00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:23.950
Shuji.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.760
Go! Come on!

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.320
Oh no!

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.760
Osaka sector-scramble

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:51.850
No...

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:04.960
In order to let you keep dreaming, I shall protect the night.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:22.410
No!

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.510
Osaka is under attack!

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.280
Please scramble.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.020
Please scramble!

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:35.620
No...I don't want to...

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:39.990
Please!

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:42.760
Let me go!

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.560
Only you can save our people!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.230
Please!

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:53.170
If you don't fight, they'll attack here next!

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:42.290
I'll be waiting there.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.220
I'll be waiting.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:52.370
<i>Shuji...</i>

00:08:52.730 --> 00:08:54.220
<i>Shuji.</i>

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:59.500
<i>Shuji...</i>

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:03.640
<i>I'll be waiting for you</i> <i>at the middle school.</i>

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:07.640
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.450
A dream...

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:50.620
Shuji...

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:52.860
Sorry...

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:56.890
Um...

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:05.340
Dummy.

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:10.970
'Morning.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:17.970
'Morning!

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:25.580
You must be tired. Go home and sleep.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.510
<i>Just like any other morning...</i>

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:44.270
<i>we walked together up</i> <i>the hill to school.</i>

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:49.740
<i>We acted as if nothing</i> <i>had happened that day...</i>

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:54.050
<i>So as not to widen</i> <i>the distance between us.</i>

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:57.890
Sure is hot today, huh Shuji?

00:10:58.560 --> 00:10:59.620
Yeah.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:04.270
Feels like it's still summer.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:05.300
Yeah.

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:08.160
You know, Shuji...

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:08.900
Yeah.

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:12.170
About the other day...

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:13.130
Yeah.

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.010
uh...

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.700
um...

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:35.020
so I was thinking if you...

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.030
Shuji?

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:41.800
Ms. Fuyumi...

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.170
"Ms. Fuyumi"?

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:58.850
<i>Shuji...</i>

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:01.520
<i>Shuji.</i>

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:05.890
<i>We shouldn't have done this...</i>

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:07.490
<i>Ms. Fuyumi...</i>

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:13.290
<i>Sorry, we can't go back</i> <i>now, can we?</i>

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:19.270
<i>We're in this together, Shuji...</i>

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:21.310
<i>Shuji...</i>

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.000
Shuji!

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.710
Akemi, don't scare me like that!

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:33.710
Brings back memories, doesn't it?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.750
Give me that!

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:39.760
You lech. Staring at me in those bloomers like that...

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:44.470
Who said I was looking at you?!

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:48.890
Then who were you looking at?

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:55.830
I'll never understand boys.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:59.710
Why would you keep an old photo like that?

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:04.310
Shut up. You wouldn't know what being in love is like.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:12.820
Sorry.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:14.890
What for?

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:19.530
I just don't want Chise to get hurt.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:23.230
Why so serious all of a sudden?

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:29.270
Chise's noticed something. She says you're acting weird.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:31.970
Like spaced out.

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.950
She asked me who this Fuyumi person was.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.950
What did you say about her?

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:42.390
Nothing!

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:50.130
I saw someone on Hell Hill who looked like her.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:53.430
She passed me on a bicycle.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:56.480
Our eyes met.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:58.600
And so...

00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:02.510
I started to wonder what she'd looked like.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:07.800
You should be telling things like this to Chise!

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:10.680
It's important you talk to her!

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:13.680
Be quiet! What do you know?!

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:19.320
MILK

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:25.430
What are you doing, Atsushi, sneaking up on me, like that?

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:27.600
Oh, thank you.

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:32.200
"How long will he carry a torch for her, the fool?"

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.600
Hey! I'll kick your ass for that!

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:37.800
That's a quote...

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:39.640
from A-ke-mi.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:47.050
It's none of her business. You'd think she was my mom!

00:14:54.900 --> 00:15:01.030
<i>It wasn't Ms. Fuyumi that</i> <i>had me out of sorts.</i>

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:23.410
<i>That night I asked her to</i> <i>run away with me...</i>

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:25.920
<i>Chise didn't come.</i>

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.790
<i>I wanted to ask...</i>

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:32.660
<i>"Chise, why didn't you show?"</i>

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:37.070
<i>But I decided to let it go.</i>

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:42.030
<i>It's better not to ask.</i> <i>She had enough of her own troubles.</i>

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:47.680
<i>But, were Chise and I...</i>

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:53.050
<i>really, truly in love?</i>

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.770
Say, Chise...

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.530
What's wrong?!

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:03.430
It's coming.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:08.130
There, see?

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:12.320
How did you know before your pager went off?

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:16.300
I don't like to scramble in broad daylight like this.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:17.800
Must hurry!

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:19.840
Wait a sec! Hold on!

00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:23.140
Don't do it in the middle of the street!

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.280
But, if I don't hurry...

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.180
people will die...

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:32.680
Over there! That house is empty!

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:34.590
Where?

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.200
There, where that truck is parked.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:39.700
No one will see you launch from there.

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:42.800
No, wait!

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:44.700
Sorry...

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:46.930
Stay here, OK?

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:51.940
I'm embarrassed, so don't watch.

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.810
OK, OK, just go!

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:10.590
That dummy...

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:19.170
<i>Wow, what a mess!</i> <i>At least no one got hurt...</i>

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:20.900
<i>Oh no!</i>

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.800
A...are you alright?!

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:26.740
Yes...

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.310
I just fell off my bike.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:30.050
Ow!

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:31.810
Can you stand?

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:36.760
A girl...she was running by...

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:41.790
<i>She saw! What'll I do now?!</i>

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.360
Shuji?

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:48.000
Shuji, right?

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.370
Shuji!

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:53.870
Ms. Fuyumi...

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:56.270
It really is you!

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:59.850
Ms. Fuyumi...what are you...

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:03.780
Look how tall you've grown!

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:07.780
You were so little in middle school.

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:12.420
The other day I saw you, but thought, "It couldn't be."

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:23.400
Things seem to get worse and worse.

00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:27.160
A gas explosion on a quiet residential street.

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:32.440
We moved here because my husband said it was safer.

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:36.850
But this is a military town.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:39.350
What a fast disaster response!

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:43.280
Makes me proud to be a soldier's wife.

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:53.200
You haven't changed, Shuji. Still the silent type.

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:06.270
Oh, come now!

00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:11.150
You aren't going to blush just looking at a woman's legs!

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:12.230
Excuse me!

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:15.850
You'll make me blush too...

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:25.830
It sure is hot, don't you think?

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:27.590
Yes.

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:33.130
I'll open a window.

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:34.370
Ouch!

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:42.240
Makes your heart pound, doesn't it?

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:43.980
No!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:45.210
Huh?

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:47.510
I have a girlfriend!

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:52.970
I know!

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:55.520
But it doesn't matter!

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:57.290
Doesn't matter?!

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:01.650
It's not fair to her or your husband!

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:06.040
It's his fault anyway...

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:14.280
Tetsu hasn't been home in almost two months.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:16.280
Shuji...

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:18.850
I get so lonely!

00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:23.620
Just for a little while...

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:26.630
lie down beside me...

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:03.560
<i>Shuji, I'm sorry.</i>

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:06.200
<i>My body...</i>

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.400
<i>won't go back the way it was.</i>

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:21.110
<i>To be precise, it can't go back.</i>

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:28.480
<i>The night you asked me</i> <i>to run away with you...</i>

00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:31.950
<i>and I didn't show up...</i>

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:35.090
<i>something in me broke.</i>

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:41.870
<i>The mechanic says I'll never</i> <i>be the way I was again.</i>

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:06.960
<i>Looking back, that day</i> <i>I saw Ms. Fuyumi...</i>

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:11.130
<i>I forgot about Chise</i> <i>for a while.</i>

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:16.100
<i>And to be honest...</i>

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:20.000
<i>it felt a little easier</i> <i>with her forgotten.</i>

00:22:24.350 --> 00:22:27.470
<i>Was that cruel of me, I wonder...</i>

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:43.420
A rift opened up upon my heart

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:49.990
And I went through the night sleepless, sighing constantly

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:59.340
Before I realize, it's turned to morning

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:08.660
I want to hear your voice

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:13.250
I want to feel your warmth

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:19.460
Thoughts of you well up within me

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:25.310
And my tears begin to overflow

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:36.570
Goodbye my beloved, I am still unable to forget about you

00:23:36.730 --> 00:23:46.740
Having all of this end with just a single word of goodbye

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:51.570
Fills me with sorrow

00:24:01.180 --> 00:24:03.910
Chise, there's nothing between me and Ms. Fuyumi anymore.

00:24:03.980 --> 00:24:06.950
I'm sure you're the one I love.

00:24:07.680 --> 00:24:10.150
Chise! Tomorrow, let's go on a date!

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:14.980
SAIKANO, Episode 4: "Fuyumi"
